Well, I'm only a mid-level player (I have ascended repeatedly, but
there are many better players) but this is the way I see it:

Trap avoidance is better.  A ring of levitation, for example, will
avoid trap doors, webs, pit traps and a bunch of other things.  Ring
of TC control negates danger of teleport traps. If you walk around
barehanded and only w)ield a weapon when you're ready to fight, rust
traps won't damage your weapon.  If you wear elvish hats and boots and
a cloak, it won't damage your armor either.

Ring of poly control negates danger of polymorph traps.  To a lesser
extent, so does dragon armor, since it guarantees what you will
transform into.  Although you lose a lot of your armor.

Also, we have that nifty dog to walk ahead of us.  When I get to a
level, simply let
the pet do the scouting and step only where the pet steps.

By the time one arrives at gehennom, searching is a waste of turns,
and I already take too long as it is.        The only time I use
search is when I want to exercise wisdom by finding a secret door or
something. Or in the Gnomish mines, where a  magic trap or a poly trap
or a trapdoor can result in a rapid death.  But even there, pet
scouting is more effective.


